# Epic Games

> Epic Games develops Unreal Engine and Fortnite and operates the Epic Games Store. This is a federated index of Epic Games' games, creation tools, marketplaces, and developer services. Entries whose URL ends in /llms.txt link a machine-readable file maintained by the team that owns that property; the rest link the property's site because it does not publish one yet.

## Creation tools and engines

- [Unreal Engine](https://www.unrealengine.com/llms.txt): Real-time 3D creation tool for games, film, architecture, and simulation.
- [Twinmotion](https://www.twinmotion.com/llms.txt): Real-time architectural and immersive visualization tool built on Unreal Engine.
- [MetaHuman](https://www.metahuman.com/llms.txt): Framework and tools for creating and animating high-fidelity digital humans.
- [RealityScan](https://www.realityscan.com/llms.txt): Photogrammetry software for creating 3D models from photos and scans.
- [Unreal Editor for Fortnite](https://create.fortnite.com/): Tools for building and publishing games and experiences in Fortnite. No llms.txt yet.

## Marketplaces and content

- [Fab](https://www.fab.com/): Unified marketplace for 3D models, materials, and digital content for creators.
- [Quixel](https://quixel.com/llms.txt): Megascans library of scanned 3D assets and materials (now part of Fab).
- [ArtStation](https://www.artstation.com/): Portfolio platform and marketplace for games, film, media, and entertainment artists. No llms.txt yet.
- [Sketchfab](https://sketchfab.com/): Platform to publish, share, and buy or sell 3D, VR, and AR content. No llms.txt yet.

## Legal, company, and player support

- [Epic Games legal documents](https://legal.epicgames.com/sitemap.xml): Terms of service, privacy policy, EULAs, and store and creator policies. XML sitemap; the domain root redirects away. No llms.txt yet.
- [Epic Games company site](https://www.epicgames.com/site): Company news, careers, security disclosures, and corporate information. No llms.txt yet.
- [Epic Games player support](https://www.epicgames.com/help/): Self-service help for accounts, purchases, refunds, and supported games. No llms.txt yet.

## Store and games

- [Epic Games Store](https://store.epicgames.com/): Digital storefront for PC games and apps, including weekly free games. No llms.txt yet.
- [Fortnite](https://www.fortnite.com/): Epic's free-to-play battle royale, creative, and social entertainment platform. No llms.txt yet.
- [Rocket League](https://www.rocketleague.com/): Free-to-play competitive game blending soccer with vehicular acrobatics. No llms.txt yet.
- [Fall Guys](https://www.fallguys.com/): Free-to-play massively multiplayer party game and obstacle-course competition. No llms.txt yet.

## Developer platform and services

- [Epic Online Services](https://onlineservices.epicgames.com/llms.txt): Free cross-platform backend services for multiplayer games.
- [Epic for developers](https://dev.epicgames.com/llms.txt): Developer documentation, community, and portal for Epic technologies.
- [Kids Web Services](https://www.kidswebservices.com/llms.txt): Age verification and parental-consent tools for COPPA and GDPR-K compliance.
- [Kids Web Services support](https://support.kidswebservices.com/llms.txt): Parent and player help center for KWS consent and account questions.
- [Lore](https://lore.org/llms.txt): Open source version control system built for source code alongside large binary assets.
- [Easy Anti-Cheat](https://www.easy.ac/llms.txt): Anti-cheat service that protects multiplayer PC games from cheating and tampering.

